Drop std::pmr from KRecentFilesAction so the build runs on macOS 13.

std::pmr lives in the libc++ dylib and Apple only shipped it in macOS 14, so a
binary that references it dies at launch on anything older with

    Symbol not found: __ZNSt3__13pmr15memory_resourceD2Ev
    Referenced from: libKF6ConfigWidgets.6.29.0.dylib
    Expected in:     /usr/lib/libc++.1.dylib

The deployment target is set to 13.3 and did not prevent this, so libc++'s
availability annotations are switched off somewhere up the toolchain — which
means the compiler will not catch the next one of these either. tests/macos-abi
checks the built bundle for exactly that.

Nothing is lost by the change: the arena existed to keep a de-duplication set of
at most m_maxItems URLs off the heap while the recent-files list is read. The
insert() call is untouched, std::set returns the same pair<iterator, bool>, and
<set> was already included.

Present in 6.28.0 as well, so pinning the framework a version back does not help.

--- a/src/krecentfilesaction.cpp
+++ b/src/krecentfilesaction.cpp
@@ -35,7 +35,6 @@
 #include <KLocalizedString>
 #include <KShell>
 
-#include <memory_resource>
 #include <set>
 
 KRecentFilesAction::KRecentFilesAction(QObject *parent)
@@ -342,9 +341,7 @@
         cg = KConfigGroup(cg.config(), QStringLiteral("RecentFiles"));
     }
 
-    std::byte memory[sizeof(QUrl) * 32];
-    std::pmr::monotonic_buffer_resource resource(memory, sizeof(memory));
-    std::pmr::set<QUrl> seenUrls(&resource);
+    std::set<QUrl> seenUrls;
 
     bool thereAreEntries = false;
